end":331,"description":"Omega-N-methylarginine; by PRMT1; alternate"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":340,"end":340,"description":"Dimethylated arginine; in A2780 ovarian carcinoma cell line"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":340,"end":340,"description":"Omega-N-methylarginine; by PRMT1"},{"type":"Region","start":351,"end":443,"description":"Interaction with HNRNPA1"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":387,"end":387,"description":"Phosphotyrosine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":390,"end":390,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Region","start":400,"end":420,"description":"Interaction with ZBTB7A"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":432,"end":432,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in SUMO2)"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":435,"end":435,"description":"Phosphotyrosine; by PTK6"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":440,"end":440,"description":"Phosphotyrosine; by PTK6"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":443,"end":443,"description":"Phosphotyrosine; by PTK6"}],"interfaces":{"KHDRBS1":[103,106,107,110,113,114,117,118,119,120,121,124,125,128,144,145,146,147,148,149,156,157,158,159,160,161,163,216,224,225,226,228,237,238,241,242,244,245,248,249,251,252,255,256],"KHDRBS2":[103,106,107,109,110,113,114,117,118,119,120,121,123,124,125,128,144,145,146,147,148,149,154,156,158,159,160,161,163,173,177,178,180,181,182,184,185,202,203,204,208,212,220,222,223,224,225,226,228,237,238,241,242,244,245,248,252,255,256,271,275]},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Self-associates to form homooligomers when bound to RNA, oligomerization appears to be limited when binding to proteins; dimerization increases RNA affinity (PubMed:20610388, PubMed:26758068). Forms a trimeric complex in the nucleus consisting of BANP, HDAC6 and KHDRBS1/SAM68; HDAC6 keeps KHDRBS1 in a deacetylated state which inhibits the inclusion of CD44 alternate exons (PubMed:26080397). The complex is disrupted by MAPK1/MAPK3-mediated phosphorylation of BANP which results in BANP export to the cytoplasm (PubMed:26080397). This facilitates acetylation of KHDRBS1 and CD44 variant exon inclusion (PubMed:26080397). Interacts with KHDRBS3/SLIM-2 (PubMed:10332027). Interacts with KHDRBS2/SLIM-1; heterooligomer formation of KHDRBS family proteins may modulate RNA substrate specificity (By similarity). Interacts with RASA1, LCK, FYN, PTPN6, PLCG1, GRB2, CBL, JAK3, PIK3R, STAT3, APC, HNRNPA1 (PubMed:10332027, PubMed:11585385, PubMed:1374686, PubMed:17371836, PubMed:22000517, PubMed:9045636). Interacts with PTK6 (via SH3 and SH2 domains) (PubMed:10913193). Forms a complex with ILF2, ILF3, YLPM1, RBMX, NCOA5 and PPP1CA (PubMed:17890166). Does not interact with TPR (PubMed:22253824). Interacts with PRMT1 (By similarity). Binds WBP4/FBP21 (via WW domains), FNBP4/FBP30 (via WW domains). Interacts (via Arg/Gly-rich-flanked Pro-rich regions) with FYN (via the SH3 domain) (By similarity). Interacts with the non-receptor tyrosine kinase SRMS; the interaction leads to phosphorylation of KHDRBS1 (PubMed:29496907). Interacts with ZBTB7A; negatively regulates KHDRBS1 splicing activity toward BCL2L1 (PubMed:24514149)"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"Q07666-2","name":"2","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"length":418,"transcripts":{"ensembl":[],"refseq":[],"refseqProteins":[],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,36],[37,62,382]],"edits":[{"start":37,"end":61,"original":"QPPLPHRSRGGGGGSRGGARASPAT","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":25,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsent":0,"foldedMissing":0,"features":[[4,1,0],[5,1,0],[6,1,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q07666-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q07666-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":65.7,"plddt":[[0,1],[50,1],[0,1],[50,4],[0,3],[50,2],[0,1],[50,1],[0,2],[50,1],[0,3],[50,3],[0,2],[50,3],[0,1],[50,1],[0,2],[50,1],[0,2],[50,2],[70,1],[50,4],[70,1],[50,1],[0,1],[50,1],[0,1],[50,2],[0,1],[50,3],[0,2],[50,4],[0,2],[50,3],[0,9],[50,3],[70,3],[90,11],[70,5],[90,1],[70,2],[